From 538198cd9926eecb6e33403ad41aa54a9f961d4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:11:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-300: F-141 3b: precise Q4_K/Q5_K MMVQ dot moves to its
 own SPIR-V (*_prec_q8_1_f32), iq3_s stock shape under
 GGML_ARIFI_MMV_ROWSTABLE_N

Cell 25 refuted 0785b7b9b9's "default 0 = unchanged": with the flag unset, the op tool lost 28 cell-24 RED rows (q4_K k=2560/3072,
q5_K n=5/8) and qwen4exp Q4_K MMVQ n=1 hashes moved (t=644 bed0e37284dd1839 -> 953d7687387a9683). The default SPIR-V path
carried no NoContraction (40 of 80 OpFSub decorated = the dead branch only), so the move happened in the driver compile of the
spec-constant branch (ASSUMED: both arms merged before the branch folded). Spec constant 5 is removed; mul_mat_vecq.comp is
byte-equal to eb750cbf9b and the default q4_k/q5_k q8_1 SPIR-V is the pre-0785b7b9b9 one. The precise dot is an

iq3_s (cell 25 T-MV8: RED at n=3/5/8 only, every shape): the lane-209 TPB16 split (16 invocations, NL=2, per-l fma into temp)
ran at NUM_COLS == 3 and > 4 only. Spec constant 4 ARIFI_IQ3_TPB_STOCK = 1 keeps the stock 8/4 shape for widths <= N
(f32 and f16 B pipelines; the id pipeline is NUM_COLS 1). Default 0 = unchanged (receipt cell 26).

Do NOT cherry-pick 0785b7b9b9 alone; this commit supersedes its shader half. Lane: lane-300

Origin: lane-300
Measured-effect: correctness only, opt-in; default restored (cache/determinism-x1-lane/cells/c26-10061224-state.json Q-FX bed0e37284dd1839, O-FX 9ec22b32739bffed; served cache/determinism-x1-lane/cells/c27-10061355-state.json); opt-in cost not measured
